#### Article 23

Every person who hears, sees, or knows of the occurrence of Violence as referred to in Article 22 is obliged to make efforts to:  
a. prevent the continuation of criminal acts;  
b. provide Protection to victims of acts of Violence;  
c. provide emergency assistance; and/or  
d. assist in the process of submitting an application for the determination of Protection.

## Part Two

Prevention of Acts of Violence

#### Article 24

1. Regional Government conducts prevention of Violence against Women and Children by means of:  
a. socializing laws and regulations;  
b. providing counseling/guidance;  
c. providing education on the dangers of domestic Violence;  
d. conducting seminars/workshops or the like;  
e. forming work networks in efforts to prevent Violence;  
f. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of Violence prevention based on partnership patterns;  
g. forming a Violence prevention system, mapping locations or areas prone to the occurrence of Violence; and h. increasing Community awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms and morality.  
2. In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:  
a. family and/or closest relatives;  
b. Community;  
c. educational institutions;  
d. health institutions;  
e. social Community institutions; and  
f. business world and other institutions.

#### Article 25

1. Regional Government is obliged to prepare prevention programs or activities as referred to in Article 24 paragraph (1) in the Regional Work Plan and Regional Strategic Plan.  
2. Programs or activities as referred to in paragraph (1) are to support the realization of the Regional Long-Term Development Plan and Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.

## Part Three

Integrated Services for Victims of Acts of Violence

#### Article 26

1. Regional Government implements Integrated Services for Women and Children victims of acts of Violence through activities:  
a. complaint Services;  
b. health Services;  
c. counseling;  
d. spiritual guidance;  
e. social Rehabilitation Services;  
f. legal aid and Assistance Services; and/or  
g. repatriation and Reintegration.  
2. Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported by facilities in the form of:  
a. special Service rooms in police lines;  
b. expert and professional personnel;  
c. Service centers and safe houses; and/or  
d. other facilities and infrastructure needed for victim recovery.  
3. Implementation of Services to victims of acts of Violence is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with P2TP2A with other social institutions.  
4. P2TP2A and other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (3) may receive and send case referrals from other Service units in a networked manner.  
5. Integrated Services for victims of acts of Violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) through (4) are implemented in accordance with Standard Operating Procedures.

#### Article 27

Procedures and procedures for Protection of Women and Children victims of Violence are further regulated by Regent Regulation.

# CHAPTER V

STRENGTHENING AND DEVELOPMENT OF INSTITUTIONS PROVIDING PROTECTION SERVICES FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 28

In the context of Protection of Women and Children, in the Region are formed:  
a. Integrated Service Center, in the form of Integrated Service Center for Women Empowerment and Child Protection (P2TP2A);  
b. Child Protection Institution (LPA); and  
c. other institutions according to needs and/or provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 29

1. P2TP2A as referred to in Article 28 letter a functions as a coordinative institution among Regional Government, law enforcement apparatus, service institutions, educational institutions, Legal Aid institutions, individuals, private sector and/or NGOs, which have capacity in Protection of Women and Children.  
2. The duties of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) include:  
a. providing Services, including:  
1\. preparing and developing information related to Women and Children and coordinating to all Regencies and reporting to the Province/Province of West Nusa Tenggara;  
2\. developing a central database obtained from the Region regarding the condition of Violence against Women and Children;  
3\. receiving complaints both in writing and orally;  
4\. conducting Services, mediation and Assistance to victims of Violence against Women and Children;  
5\. conducting education/training; and  
6\. coordinating with related institutions/individuals both in other Regencies/Cities, Provincial Government in the context of providing Protection to Women and Children.  
b. providing Protection to victims of acts of Violence, reporters and witnesses.  
3. Appointment of P2TP2A management as referred to in paragraph (1) is determined by Regent Decree.  
4. P2TP2A is under the coordination of SKPD or work unit that handles women empowerment and Child Protection.

#### Article 30

1. In order to increase the effectiveness of Implementation of Child Protection, the Regent forms LPA as referred to in Article 28 letter b which is independent in nature.  
2.	LPA as referred to in paragraph (1) has the duty to:  
a.	conduct Supervision of the implementation of Protection and fulfillment of Children's rights;  
b.	provide input and proposals in the formulation of policies regarding Implementation of Child Protection;  
c.	collect data and information regarding Child Protection;  
d.	receive and conduct examination of Community complaints regarding violations of Children's rights;  
e.	conduct mediation on disputes regarding violations of Children's rights;  
f.	conduct cooperation with Community institutions, Government and NGOs in the form of work networks, for the fulfillment and Protection of Children's rights; and  
g.	conduct handling activities on cases of violations and neglect of Children's rights.

# CHAPTER VI

## PARTICIPATION

## Part One

Community Participation

#### Article 31

1. Community may participate in Protection of Women and Children.  
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out in the form of:  
a. assisting Regional Government in the form of Supervision of Protection of Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;  
b. reporting to the competent authorities if they know Women and Children who experience Violence; and  
c. participating in the process of prevention, recovery, Rehabilitation, Reintegration and Empowerment of victims.

## Part Two

Child Participation

#### Article 32

1. Every Child has the right to participate in expressing opinions, ideas, thoughts and others and be involved in decision-making processes concerning their lives either directly or indirectly, which are implemented with the consent and will of all Children based on awareness and understanding, in accordance with age and level of thinking maturity.  
2. Child Participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out through Child Forum/Child Council starting from Village, Sub-district, and Regency levels.  
3. Child Forum/Child Council as referred to in paragraph (2) is a representation of Children, both representation of Children's geographical domicile, Children's socio-cultural groups, Children with special needs and Children's educational background.  
4. Formation of Child Forum/Child Council as referred to in paragraph (2) is facilitated by Regional Government.  
5. Formation of Child Forum/Child Council as referred to in paragraph (3) is determined by Regent Decree.

#### Article 33

Funding sources for Child Forum/Child Council may come from:  
a. donations from Community/Business Entities that are non-binding in nature;  
b. assistance from Regional Government; and/or  
c. other funding sources in accordance with laws and regulations.
